# From turns_spring_1600_events' output (France, Spring 1600, turn 108). Fixture edits (sav_json):
# England <-> France at peace (euro_relation 96 both ways), the Caravel sailing to Europe (unit 148)
# given 15 turns left, every idle / sentried / go-to French unit on the map Fortified (order 6), then
#   unit 83 (Free Colonist in Guadeloupe (41,24)) Go To Quebec (45,24): orders 3, goto (45,24);
#   unit 79 (Caravel in Quebec) Go To Port Montreal (43,27): orders 3, goto (43,27).
# Covers: Go To orders playing out over two ended turns. The colonist walks the roads out of
# Guadeloupe to (44,26) in Spring 1600 and reaches Quebec in Autumn 1600, where the order clears and
# he asks for orders (Fortify). The Caravel sails out in Spring 1600 (keys pressed while a Go To
# runs are dropped, so the end-turn Space no longer cuts its route short) and docks in Montreal in
# Autumn 1600 (order cleared); in Spring 1601 it asks for orders there.
# Returns pressed while the AI turn runs are eaten by its nested polls (one per turn here), so
# each turn's popup chain gets one Return more than it has popups; shots confirm the state.
wait 40                   # Spring 1600: the go-to pacer walks the colonist, then sails the Caravel
key space                  # end turn 108
wait 60
key Return                 # (eaten while the AI turn runs)
wait 30
key Return                 # Help: Time Scale (two turns per year from 1600)
wait 30
key Return                 # SoL in Quebec up to 60%: Continue turn
wait 30
key Return                 # price of Cigars rises
wait 30
shot                       # Autumn 1600: colonist 84 has arrived in Quebec, go-to cleared, asks for orders
key f                      # Fortify him
wait 30
shot
key space                  # end turn 109
wait 60
key Return                 # Iroquois gift of 16 Ore to Port au Prince
wait 12
key Return                 # King raises tax to 27%: Kiss pinky ring
wait 12
key Return                 # SoL in Port au Prince 12%: Continue turn
wait 12
key Return                 # SoL in Martinique 51%: Continue turn
wait 12
key Return                 # SoL in Guadeloupe 70%: Continue turn
wait 12
key Return                 # Horses cargo ready at Montreal (warehouse full): Continue turn
wait 30
shot                       # Spring 1601: the Caravel, docked in Montreal, asks for orders
